No open findings remain. I found and fixed three review issues during the workflow:

1. High: [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js) could leave the new locality panel empty when `localMap.nearbyReferences` narrowed to `[]`. The presenter now backfills calm named references from map nodes so the board still shows usable nearby names.
2. Medium: [LocalityReferencePanel.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/LocalityReferencePanel.tsx) ignored `viewModel.heading` and hardcoded the heading. It now uses the presenter-provided heading, so the seam is actually reusable.
3. Medium: the story artifact was out of sync. [5-3-add-concrete-nearby-station-and-locality-references.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/5-3-add-concrete-nearby-station-and-locality-references.md) now includes a `Senior Developer Review (AI)` section and is marked `done`, and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml) is synced to `done`.

I added regression coverage in [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs) for the fallback locality-reference path and for the panel consuming `viewModel.heading`.

Validation passed: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test -- --runInBand`, and `npm run build`.
